# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# La Sabrosita production workspace
#
# Rule of thumb: client SOURCE media belongs in this repo (through Git
# LFS). Anything a machine can regenerate does not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Rendered video and render output ------------------------------
# TV renders and Remotion output are regenerated from code plus the
# masters, so the code and the masters are what deserve version
# history. A single 4K render is larger than every asset in this repo
# combined, and it changes on every run.
#
# This is a blanket rule on purpose. If the client ever hands over real
# SOURCE footage that has to be kept, add it deliberately with
# `git add -f` and add a matching line to .gitattributes so it goes
# through LFS instead of landing in Git as a raw blob.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.avi
*.mkv
*.prores
*.mxf

# Remotion / render output directories
motion/out/
motion/build/
motion/.remotion/
out/
build/
dist/

# HyperFrames render output that is NOT video, and therefore slipped past
# the blanket *.mp4 rule above: the frame snapshots and contact sheets the
# CLI writes while a composition is being reviewed. They are the same class
# of thing as a render — regenerated from the code and the masters by
#   npx hyperframes snapshot --at <times> -o renders/<name>
# and one review pass of the 39-product reel writes ~350 MB of them.
#
# The directory itself is kept (renders/.gitkeep is tracked) so the path
# exists on a fresh clone.
#
# `**/` is load-bearing: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to THIS
# file's directory, so a bare `renders/*` would only ever match a renders/
# folder at the repo root — not tv-menu/motion/hyperframes/renders/, which
# is the one that fills up.
**/renders/*
!**/renders/.gitkeep

# HyperFrames Studio's preview thumbnail cache. 1,099 files after one
# session, rewritten on every preview, useful to nobody but the local
# Studio instance.
.thumbnails/

# HyperFrames tool scratch: animation maps, frame packets, diagnostics.
# Regenerated on demand from the compositions
#   node <skill>/scripts/animation-map.mjs . --out .hyperframes/anim-map
# and a single animation map of the 39-product reel is 1.4 MB of sampled
# bounding boxes — an analysis OF the source, never the source.
.hyperframes/

# --- Dependencies --------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.yarn/
bower_components/

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------
# Never. Not even "temporarily". This repo is private, but private is
# not the same as safe — every collaborator and every clone gets them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
credentials.json
secrets.json
service-account*.json

# --- OS junk -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.VolumeIcon.icns
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Temporary and working files -----------------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.log
.cache/
.tmp/
tmp/
scratch/

# Adobe / editor scratch — the working file is not the deliverable
*.psb
*.aep
Adobe Premiere Pro Auto-Save/
Adobe After Effects Auto-Save/

# --- Editor / tooling ----------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace

# Local Claude Code settings are per-machine, not project state
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Explicitly NOT ignored ----------------------------------------
# assets/** is the point of this repo. It is tracked through Git LFS,
# configured in .gitattributes. Do not add an assets/ ignore rule.
